course: dictionary
lesson: 2895
title: Doubt: not sure, or not trusting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Doubt can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a doubt is a feeling of not being sure: «He had doubts about the new plan.» As a verb, to doubt means to feel unsure that something is true, or to think it is probably not true: «I doubt it will rain» means you think rain is unlikely.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «If people make you doubt yourself, trust what you know.» Here doubt means to feel unsure about yourself. Noah «lent» his card to a kid who said he'd lost it, then saw him trading it, so Noah began to doubt him, which means he no longer trusted or believed him.
explain: Some useful phrases: «no doubt» means surely, «without a doubt» means certainly, «in doubt» means not sure yet, and «benefit of the doubt» means believing someone even though you are not completely sure. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: As a noun, doubt means a feeling of not being sure.
fact: As a verb, doubt can mean feeling unsure that something is true, or not trusting someone.
fact: «No doubt» means surely, and «without a doubt» means certainly.
fact: «If in doubt, throw it away» means if you are not sure, it is safer to throw it out.
fact: In science, doubt is healthy: if you doubt an answer, check it again.
exercise: «I doubt it will rain today,» said Sam. What does doubt mean here? | *To think it is probably not true | To shout loudly across a field | To trust someone with a secret | To feel completely sure it is true
exercise: «Some historians doubt the experiment happened as told.» What does this suggest? | They are certain it happened exactly as told | They have never heard of the experiment | *They are not sure it happened as told | They are planning to repeat it tomorrow
exercise: «Without a doubt, the sun rises in the east.» What does «without a doubt» mean? | Maybe | Slowly | Not at all | *Certainly
test: «He had doubts about the new plan.» What is a doubt in this sentence? | *A feeling of not being sure | A loud noise | A plan that is finished | A kind of fruit
test: Noah saw the boy trading his card, so he began to doubt him. What does doubt mean? | To feel very happy about him | To lend him a card | *Not to trust or believe him | To forget his name
exam: «If in doubt, throw it away.» What does «in doubt» mean? | Happy to keep it | *Not sure | Very sure | Hidden under the table
